    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d515">

                <pb facs="0684" n="670" sameAs="frus:frus1945v09/pg670"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">462.00R/9–2745: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Berle</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-09-27T15:00:00-03:00">September 27,
                            1945—3 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 9:54 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2983. In conversation with Velloso last night question of Brazilian share of
                    German reparations came up.<anchor n="18" xml:id="d515-f1"/> Text of Braz. note
                    in answer <pb facs="0685" n="671" xml:id="pg671"/> to ours is being
                        forwarded.<anchor n="19" xml:id="d515-f2"/> Velloso’s position is that no
                    arrangement determining Brazil’s share of German reparations is binding unless
                    Braz. is party to the discussions. Fact, of course, is Brazil does not take
                    kindly to determination of her affairs by two or three powers without
                    consultation. Velloso agrees, however, that question is academic because of fact
                    there is no way of collecting reparations and that by comparison with claims of
                    other countries blocked assets here probably give Brazil as good a position
                    proportionatey as she can expect.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berle</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d515-f1" n="18" xml:id="d515-f1-content">
                <p>For documentation relating to the subject of German reparations and restitution,
                    see <ref target="frus1945v03#pg_1169">vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">iii</hi>,
                        pp. 1169</ref> ff.; for text of specific instructions sent to Brazil in
                    regard thereto, see telegram 2089, August 28, 9 a.m., <ref
                        target="frus1945v03#pg_1266">vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">iii</hi>, p.
                        1266</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d515-f2" n="19" xml:id="d515-f2-content">
                <p>Copy transmitted to the Department in despatch 2971, September 27, from Rio de
                    Janeiro, not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
